cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GBin in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GBin: Ultra-fast GPU-accelerated metagenomic binning"
abstract: >-
  GBin is a hybrid, GPU-accelerated metagenomic binner. A self-supervised
  variational autoencoder embeds contigs from tetranucleotide composition and
  per-sample abundance; single-copy marker genes add cannot-link constraints and
  decontaminate bins; the latent space is clustered on the GPU. CheckM2 can be
  used for accurate final QC and for guided decontamination of contaminated bins.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ruochen
    family-names: Chao
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-06"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RosieCaTT/GBin.git"
url: "https://github.com/RosieCaTT/GBin"
keywords:
  - metagenomics
  - genome binning
  - metagenome-assembled genomes
  - variational autoencoder
  - GPU
  - CUDA
  - bioinformatics
